window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b397-bdab7c2f099934d9.json"]={sha256:"bdab7c2f099934d9cde8e2ab4b783caa9a5211e7c16d755f2170d87ef297049f",value:{"id":"b397","title":"跨座式單軌導梁","titleEn":"Straddle-monorail guideway beams","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦跨座導梁的彎扭變形幾何與車輛動態介面。從導梁彎曲的量級檢查建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把導梁伸縮與支承活動與導梁波長與行車激振連成可驗證的介面，最後以彎扭溫度整合案例整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies bending, torsion, geometry and vehicle dynamics of straddle-monorail beams. Start with scale check of guideway bending to define physical or information boundaries, connect thermal movement and support travel with guideway wavelength and running excitation as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through combined bending, torsion and temperature cases. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-integration","subcategoryTitle":"車站機廠與系統整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Stations depots and integration","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-integration","learningTags":["rail","rail-integration","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-integration","architectureNodes":[["車輪載重","Wheel load"],["導梁彎曲","Beam bending"],["導梁扭轉","Beam torsion"],["溫度變形","Thermal movement"],["幾何驗證","Geometry verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-integration","labels":["車輪載重","導梁彎曲","導梁扭轉","溫度變形","幾何驗證"],"labelsEn":["Wheel load","Beam bending","Beam torsion","Thermal movement","Geometry verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究導梁彎曲的量級檢查。原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。公式 y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000，代入得 y=0.761905 mm。邊界：小撓度等截面歐拉梁，簡支與單一跨中力，忽略剪切及扭轉。敏感度只改 L=20 至 22 m，輸出變為 1.0141 mm；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究偏心輪載與導梁扭轉：原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。公式 y=T*L/(G*J)*1000，代入得 y=0.428571 mrad。邊界：均勻聖維南扭轉與已知等效扭轉常數，未含翹曲拘束。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。以簡支跨中力建立導梁撓度基準，觀察跨度三次方對變形的影響。真實輪載分布和支承條件另列，避免將單一教學梁當成整條導梁驗收。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate scale check of guideway bending. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4. Formula y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000 gives y=0.761905 mm. Boundary: Small-deflection uniform Euler beam with simple supports and one central load; shear and torsion are omitted. For sensitivity, change only L=20 to 22 m; the output becomes 1.0141 mm. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate eccentric wheel loads and beam twist: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4. Formula y=T*L/(G*J)*1000 gives y=0.428571 mrad. Boundary: Uniform Saint-Venant torsion with a known equivalent torsion constant; restrained warping is excluded. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Use a simply supported central-load beam as a deflection reference and examine cubic span sensitivity. Retain real wheel distribution and supports as separate conditions rather than accepting a full guideway through one beam model. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b397-v16-s1","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查與偏心輪載與導梁扭轉","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending & Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist","description":"本階段聚焦「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」與「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scale check of guideway bending\" and \"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b397-v16-01","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scale check of guideway bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以簡支跨中力建立導梁撓度基準，觀察跨度三次方對變形的影響。真實輪載分布和支承條件另列，避免將單一教學梁當成整條導梁驗收。簡支梁跨中集中荷載的撓度隨跨度三次方增加，與彎曲剛度成反比。跨座導梁的車輛輪載並非真正集中於單點，支承與扭轉也會參與；概念梁模型適合量級檢查，但不能直接作為完整導梁的行車驗收。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：小撓度等截面歐拉梁，簡支與單一跨中力，忽略剪切及扭轉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use a simply supported central-load beam as a deflection reference and examine cubic span sensitivity. Retain real wheel distribution and supports as separate conditions rather than accepting a full guideway through one beam model. Midspan deflection of a simply supported beam under a central point load scales with span cubed and inversely with flexural rigidity. Monorail wheel loads are distributed and involve supports and torsion. The beam model is useful for scale checks, not complete guideway acceptance. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Small-deflection uniform Euler beam with simple supports and one central load; shear and torsion are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scale check of guideway bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4.","failure":"常見誤解：「跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scale check of guideway bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-01-k1","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending","text":"以簡支跨中力建立導梁撓度基準，觀察跨度三次方對變形的影響。真實輪載分布和支承條件另列，避免將單一教學梁當成整條導梁驗收。","textEn":"Use a simply supported central-load beam as a deflection reference and examine cubic span sensitivity. Retain real wheel distribution and supports as separate conditions rather than accepting a full guideway through one beam model.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scale check of guideway bending\" is correct?","options":["跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍","以簡支跨中力建立導梁撓度基準，觀察跨度三次方對變形的影響。","導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉"],"optionsEn":["Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection.","Use a simply supported central-load beam as a deflection reference and examine cubic span sensitivity.","Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以簡支跨中力建立導梁撓度基準，觀察跨度三次方對變形的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use a simply supported central-load beam as a deflection reference and examine cubic span sensitivity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b397-v16-02","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scale check of guideway bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。公式 y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000，代入得 y=0.761905 mm。邊界：小撓度等截面歐拉梁，簡支與單一跨中力，忽略剪切及扭轉。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4. Formula y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000 gives y=0.761905 mm. Boundary: Small-deflection uniform Euler beam with simple supports and one central load; shear and torsion are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量跨中與支承位移並扣除支承沉陷，以不同載重檢查線性比例及卸載回復。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure midspan and support movement, subtract support settlement, and test load proportionality and unloading recovery.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。公式 y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000，代入得 y=0.761905 mm。邊界：小撓度等截面歐拉梁，簡支與單一跨中力，忽略剪切及扭轉。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4. Formula y=P*L**3/(48*E*I)*1000 gives y=0.761905 mm. Boundary: Small-deflection uniform Euler beam with simple supports and one central load; shear and torsion are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scale check of guideway bending\", which statement holds?","options":["量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力","任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。"],"optionsEn":["No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress.","Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：跨中集中力 P=80000 N；簡支跨度 L=20 m；彈性模數 E=3.5e+10 Pa；截面慣性矩 I=0.5 m4。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: central point load P=80000 N; simply supported span L=20 m; Young modulus E=3.5e+10 Pa; second moment of area I=0.5 m4. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b397-v16-03","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scale check of guideway bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量跨中與支承位移並扣除支承沉陷，以不同載重檢查線性比例及卸載回復。以「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure midspan and support movement, subtract support settlement, and test load proportionality and unloading recovery. For scale check of guideway bending, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把簡支跨度 L 從 20 改成 22 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.761905 變為 1.0141 mm。先說明「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only simply supported span L from 20 to 22 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.761905 to 1.0141 mm. Explain the causal direction for scale check of guideway bending, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：未扣支承沉陷會把基礎移動當成梁撓度，裂縫或接頭滑移則使載重關係不再線性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unremoved support settlement appears as beam deflection; cracking or joint slip can make the load relation nonlinear. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量跨中與支承位移並扣除支承沉陷，以不同載重檢查線性比例及卸載回復。以「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure midspan and support movement, subtract support settlement, and test load proportionality and unloading recovery. For scale check of guideway bending, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把簡支跨度 L 從 20 改成 22 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.761905 變為 1.0141 mm。先說明「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only simply supported span L from 20 to 22 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.761905 to 1.0141 mm. Explain the causal direction for scale check of guideway bending, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scale check of guideway bending\"?","options":["量跨中與支承位移並扣除支承沉陷，以不同載重檢查線性比例及卸載回復。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小"],"optionsEn":["Measure midspan and support movement, subtract support settlement, and test load proportionality and unloading recovery.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量跨中與支承位移並扣除支承沉陷，以不同載重檢查線性比例及卸載回復。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure midspan and support movement, subtract support settlement, and test load proportionality and unloading recovery. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b397-v16-04","title":"導梁彎曲的量級檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scale check of guideway bending: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scale check of guideway bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未扣支承沉陷會把基礎移動當成梁撓度，裂縫或接頭滑移則使載重關係不再線性。回到「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unremoved support settlement appears as beam deflection; cracking or joint slip can make the load relation nonlinear. Trace the input chain for scale check of guideway bending. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：小撓度等截面歐拉梁，簡支與單一跨中力，忽略剪切及扭轉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Small-deflection uniform Euler beam with simple supports and one central load; shear and torsion are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未扣支承沉陷會把基礎移動當成梁撓度，裂縫或接頭滑移則使載重關係不再線性。回到「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Unremoved support settlement appears as beam deflection; cracking or joint slip can make the load relation nonlinear. Trace the input chain for scale check of guideway bending. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導梁彎曲的量級檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scale check of guideway bending\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","未扣支承沉陷會把基礎移動當成梁撓度，裂縫或接頭滑移則使載重關係不再線性。","導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unremoved support settlement appears as beam deflection; cracking or joint slip can make the load relation nonlinear.","Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未扣支承沉陷會把基礎移動當成梁撓度，裂縫或接頭滑移則使載重關係不再線性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unremoved support settlement appears as beam deflection; cracking or joint slip can make the load relation nonlinear. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b397-v16-05","title":"偏心輪載與導梁扭轉：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨座車輛偏心載重會使導梁兩側產生相對轉角，即使中心線撓度仍小。以成對高程量測檢查扭轉，區分剛體轉動、支承沉陷與截面變形。偏心輪載會扭轉導梁，扭角由扭矩、長度與扭轉剛度控制。兩側輪道相對高差會影響導向輪接觸，即使跨中垂直撓度很小仍可能存在明顯扭轉；開口截面與翹曲拘束的行為不能用單純圓軸公式概括。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻聖維南扭轉與已知等效扭轉常數，未含翹曲拘束。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Eccentric monorail loading can twist opposite guide surfaces despite small centreline deflection. Use paired elevation measurements to distinguish twist, rigid rotation and support settlement. Eccentric wheel loading twists a guideway, with angle governed by torque, length and torsional rigidity. Relative rail-surface height affects guide-wheel contact even when vertical deflection is small. Open sections and restrained warping cannot be represented fully by a simple shaft analogy. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform Saint-Venant torsion with a known equivalent torsion constant; restrained warping is excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4.","failure":"常見誤解：「導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-05-k1","title":"偏心輪載與導梁扭轉","titleEn":"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist","text":"跨座車輛偏心載重會使導梁兩側產生相對轉角，即使中心線撓度仍小。以成對高程量測檢查扭轉，區分剛體轉動、支承沉陷與截面變形。","textEn":"Eccentric monorail loading can twist opposite guide surfaces despite small centreline deflection. Use paired elevation measurements to distinguish twist, rigid rotation and support settlement.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist\" is correct?","options":["導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉","速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍","跨座車輛偏心載重會使導梁兩側產生相對轉角，即使中心線撓度仍小。"],"optionsEn":["Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur.","Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.","Eccentric monorail loading can twist opposite guide surfaces despite small centreline deflection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨座車輛偏心載重會使導梁兩側產生相對轉角，即使中心線撓度仍小。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Eccentric monorail loading can twist opposite guide surfaces despite small centreline deflection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b397-v16-06","title":"偏心輪載與導梁扭轉：定量估算","titleEn":"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。公式 y=T*L/(G*J)*1000，代入得 y=0.428571 mrad。邊界：均勻聖維南扭轉與已知等效扭轉常數，未含翹曲拘束。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4. Formula y=T*L/(G*J)*1000 gives y=0.428571 mrad. Boundary: Uniform Saint-Venant torsion with a known equivalent torsion constant; restrained warping is excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在兩側同斷面量高程差，將剛體轉動與支承沉陷分離，再比較偏心載重方向反轉。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure opposite-side elevations at common sections, separate rigid rotation and settlement, and reverse eccentric loading for comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。公式 y=T*L/(G*J)*1000，代入得 y=0.428571 mrad。邊界：均勻聖維南扭轉與已知等效扭轉常數，未含翹曲拘束。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4. Formula y=T*L/(G*J)*1000 gives y=0.428571 mrad. Boundary: Uniform Saint-Venant torsion with a known equivalent torsion constant; restrained warping is excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。","同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確","幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4.","Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position.","Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：扭矩 T=120000 N*m；構件長度 L=15 m；剪切模數 G=1.4e+10 Pa；等效扭轉常數 J=0.3 m4。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: torque T=120000 N*m; member length L=15 m; shear modulus G=1.4e+10 Pa; equivalent torsion constant J=0.3 m4. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b397-v16-07","title":"偏心輪載與導梁扭轉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在兩側同斷面量高程差，將剛體轉動與支承沉陷分離，再比較偏心載重方向反轉。以「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure opposite-side elevations at common sections, separate rigid rotation and settlement, and reverse eccentric loading for comparison. For eccentric wheel loads and beam twist, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把扭矩 T 從 120000 改成 132000 N*m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.428571 變為 0.471429 mrad。先說明「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only torque T from 120000 to 132000 N*m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.428571 to 0.471429 mrad. Explain the causal direction for eccentric wheel loads and beam twist, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只量梁中心線會漏掉扭轉，左右感測器不同基準則可能製造假的扭角。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Centreline-only measurements miss torsion; mismatched sensor datums can create an artificial twist angle. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在兩側同斷面量高程差，將剛體轉動與支承沉陷分離，再比較偏心載重方向反轉。以「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure opposite-side elevations at common sections, separate rigid rotation and settlement, and reverse eccentric loading for comparison. For eccentric wheel loads and beam twist, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把扭矩 T 從 120000 改成 132000 N*m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.428571 變為 0.471429 mrad。先說明「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only torque T from 120000 to 132000 N*m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.428571 to 0.471429 mrad. Explain the causal direction for eccentric wheel loads and beam twist, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在兩側同斷面量高程差，將剛體轉動與支承沉陷分離，再比較偏心載重方向反轉。","三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Measure opposite-side elevations at common sections, separate rigid rotation and settlement, and reverse eccentric loading for comparison.","Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在兩側同斷面量高程差，將剛體轉動與支承沉陷分離，再比較偏心載重方向反轉。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure opposite-side elevations at common sections, separate rigid rotation and settlement, and reverse eccentric loading for comparison. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b397-v16-08","title":"偏心輪載與導梁扭轉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量梁中心線會漏掉扭轉，左右感測器不同基準則可能製造假的扭角。回到「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Centreline-only measurements miss torsion; mismatched sensor datums can create an artificial twist angle. Trace the input chain for eccentric wheel loads and beam twist. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻聖維南扭轉與已知等效扭轉常數，未含翹曲拘束。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform Saint-Venant torsion with a known equivalent torsion constant; restrained warping is excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量梁中心線會漏掉扭轉，左右感測器不同基準則可能製造假的扭角。回到「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Centreline-only measurements miss torsion; mismatched sensor datums can create an artificial twist angle. Trace the input chain for eccentric wheel loads and beam twist. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偏心輪載與導梁扭轉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eccentric wheel loads and beam twist\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍","只量梁中心線會漏掉扭轉，左右感測器不同基準則可能製造假的扭角。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.","Centreline-only measurements miss torsion; mismatched sensor datums can create an artificial twist angle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只量梁中心線會漏掉扭轉，左右感測器不同基準則可能製造假的扭角。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Centreline-only measurements miss torsion; mismatched sensor datums can create an artificial twist angle. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b397-v16-s2","title":"曲線速度與側向需求與導梁伸縮與支承活動","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand & Thermal movement and support travel","description":"本階段聚焦「曲線速度與側向需求」與「導梁伸縮與支承活動」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Curve speed and lateral demand\" and \"Thermal movement and support travel\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b397-v16-09","title":"曲線速度與側向需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「曲線速度與側向需求」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Curve speed and lateral demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將曲線半徑和車速換成側向加速度量級，觀察車速平方的影響。導向輪力仍取決於車體和懸吊分配，不可把集中質點結果直接當成單輪荷載。曲線向心加速度與速度平方成正比、與半徑成反比，導向輪與懸吊需共同提供相應作用。傾斜或超高可改變乘客感受的側向分量，但不會消除車輛轉彎所需的向心加速度；轉折處的變化率亦影響舒適。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平面定速圓曲線，不含超高、傾斜與過渡曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲線速度與側向需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Convert curve radius and speed into a lateral-acceleration scale and examine the square-speed effect. Guide-wheel forces still depend on vehicle and suspension distribution, so a point-mass result is not a single-wheel load. Centripetal acceleration scales with speed squared and inverse radius, supplied through guidance and suspension forces. Tilt or banking changes the lateral component felt by passengers but does not remove the acceleration needed to turn. Its rate of change through transitions also affects comfort. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-speed planar circular curve, excluding cant, tilt and transition geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Curve speed and lateral demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：速度 v=12 m/s；曲線半徑 R=150 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: speed v=12 m/s; curve radius R=150 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲線速度與側向需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Curve speed and lateral demand”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-09-k1","title":"曲線速度與側向需求","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand","text":"將曲線半徑和車速換成側向加速度量級，觀察車速平方的影響。導向輪力仍取決於車體和懸吊分配，不可把集中質點結果直接當成單輪荷載。","textEn":"Convert curve radius and speed into a lateral-acceleration scale and examine the square-speed effect. Guide-wheel forces still depend on vehicle and suspension distribution, so a point-mass result is not a single-wheel load.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲線速度與側向需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Curve speed and lateral demand\" is correct?","options":["將曲線半徑和車速換成側向加速度量級，觀察車速平方的影響。","速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍","量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Convert curve radius and speed into a lateral-acceleration scale and examine the square-speed effect.","Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.","No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將曲線半徑和車速換成側向加速度量級，觀察車速平方的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Convert curve radius and speed into a lateral-acceleration scale and examine the square-speed effect. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b397-v16-10","title":"曲線速度與側向需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲線速度與側向需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Curve speed and lateral demand” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：速度 v=12 m/s；曲線半徑 R=150 m。公式 y=v*v/R，代入得 y=0.96 m/s2。邊界：平面定速圓曲線，不含超高、傾斜與過渡曲線。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: speed v=12 m/s; curve radius R=150 m. Formula y=v*v/R gives y=0.96 m/s2. Boundary: Constant-speed planar circular curve, excluding cant, tilt and transition geometry. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步比較速度、曲率及車體側向加速度，先轉換感測器座標再討論乘坐感受。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare synchronized speed, curvature and body lateral acceleration after transforming sensor coordinates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：速度 v=12 m/s；曲線半徑 R=150 m。公式 y=v*v/R，代入得 y=0.96 m/s2。邊界：平面定速圓曲線，不含超高、傾斜與過渡曲線。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: speed v=12 m/s; curve radius R=150 m. Formula y=v*v/R gives y=0.96 m/s2. Boundary: Constant-speed planar circular curve, excluding cant, tilt and transition geometry.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲線速度與側向需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Curve speed and lateral demand\", which statement holds?","options":["任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","原創假想教學輸入：速度 v=12 m/s；曲線半徑 R=150 m。","結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小"],"optionsEn":["Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: speed v=12 m/s; curve radius R=150 m.","A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：速度 v=12 m/s；曲線半徑 R=150 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: speed v=12 m/s; curve radius R=150 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b397-v16-11","title":"曲線速度與側向需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲線速度與側向需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Curve speed and lateral demand” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步比較速度、曲率及車體側向加速度，先轉換感測器座標再討論乘坐感受。以「曲線速度與側向需求」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare synchronized speed, curvature and body lateral acceleration after transforming sensor coordinates. For curve speed and lateral demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把速度 v 從 12 改成 13.2 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.96 變為 1.1616 m/s2。先說明「曲線速度與側向需求」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only speed v from 12 to 13.2 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.96 to 1.1616 m/s2. Explain the causal direction for curve speed and lateral demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器未扣重力投影會把傾斜誤當側向動態，曲率定位錯位則使模型峰值位置偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unremoved gravity projection can mimic lateral dynamics; misregistered curvature shifts the predicted peak location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步比較速度、曲率及車體側向加速度，先轉換感測器座標再討論乘坐感受。以「曲線速度與側向需求」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare synchronized speed, curvature and body lateral acceleration after transforming sensor coordinates. For curve speed and lateral demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把速度 v 從 12 改成 13.2 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.96 變為 1.1616 m/s2。先說明「曲線速度與側向需求」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only speed v from 12 to 13.2 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.96 to 1.1616 m/s2. Explain the causal direction for curve speed and lateral demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲線速度與側向需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Curve speed and lateral demand\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","同步比較速度、曲率及車體側向加速度，先轉換感測器座標再討論乘坐感受。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Compare synchronized speed, curvature and body lateral acceleration after transforming sensor coordinates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步比較速度、曲率及車體側向加速度，先轉換感測器座標再討論乘坐感受。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare synchronized speed, curvature and body lateral acceleration after transforming sensor coordinates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b397-v16-12","title":"曲線速度與側向需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Curve speed and lateral demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲線速度與側向需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Curve speed and lateral demand” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器未扣重力投影會把傾斜誤當側向動態，曲率定位錯位則使模型峰值位置偏移。回到「曲線速度與側向需求」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unremoved gravity projection can mimic lateral dynamics; misregistered curvature shifts the predicted peak location. Trace the input chain for curve speed and lateral demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平面定速圓曲線，不含超高、傾斜與過渡曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-speed planar circular curve, excluding cant, tilt and transition geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器未扣重力投影會把傾斜誤當側向動態，曲率定位錯位則使模型峰值位置偏移。回到「曲線速度與側向需求」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Unremoved gravity projection can mimic lateral dynamics; misregistered curvature shifts the predicted peak location. Trace the input chain for curve speed and lateral demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲線速度與側向需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Curve speed and lateral demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["感測器未扣重力投影會把傾斜誤當側向動態，曲率定位錯位則使模型峰值位置偏移。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Unremoved gravity projection can mimic lateral dynamics; misregistered curvature shifts the predicted peak location.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"感測器未扣重力投影會把傾斜誤當側向動態，曲率定位錯位則使模型峰值位置偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unremoved gravity projection can mimic lateral dynamics; misregistered curvature shifts the predicted peak location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b397-v16-13","title":"導梁伸縮與支承活動：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal movement and support travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「導梁伸縮與支承活動」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal movement and support travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"先用自由伸長估計均勻溫差下的位移需求，再比較固定與活動支承如何改變反應。日照熱梯度和支承卡滯不在此簡式內，須另保留量測證據。自由熱伸長與原長、膨脹係數及溫差成正比，但受拘束後伸長會被轉成內力。接縫、支承與鄰接構件共同決定這種轉換；因此同一個溫差可能在自由端表現為位移，在固定端表現為應力，不能用一種量測代替另一種。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻溫度與自由伸長；不包含熱梯度引起的彎曲。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導梁伸縮與支承活動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Estimate uniform-temperature free movement before comparing fixed and sliding support responses. Solar gradients and seized bearings lie outside the simple relation and need separate measurement evidence. Free thermal expansion scales with length, coefficient and temperature change, while restraint converts some expansion into force. Joints, supports and adjoining members govern that conversion. The same temperature change can produce movement at a free end and stress at a restrained end, so one measurement cannot replace the other. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform temperature and free expansion; thermal-gradient bending is omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal movement and support travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：構件長度 L=30 m；膨脹係數 alpha=1.2e-05 1/K；溫度變化 dT=20 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: member length L=30 m; expansion coefficient alpha=1.2e-05 1/K; temperature change dT=20 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal movement and support travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-13-k1","title":"導梁伸縮與支承活動","titleEn":"Thermal movement and support travel","text":"先用自由伸長估計均勻溫差下的位移需求，再比較固定與活動支承如何改變反應。日照熱梯度和支承卡滯不在此簡式內，須另保留量測證據。","textEn":"Estimate uniform-temperature free movement before comparing fixed and sliding support responses. Solar gradients and seized bearings lie outside the simple relation and need separate measurement evidence.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導梁伸縮與支承活動」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal movement and support travel\" is correct?","options":["量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力","先用自由伸長估計均勻溫差下的位移需求，再比較固定與活動支承如何改變反應。","同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確"],"optionsEn":["No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress.","Estimate uniform-temperature free movement before comparing fixed and sliding support responses.","Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先用自由伸長估計均勻溫差下的位移需求，再比較固定與活動支承如何改變反應。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Estimate uniform-temperature free movement before comparing fixed and sliding support responses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b397-v16-14","title":"導梁伸縮與支承活動：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal movement and support travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal movement and support travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：構件長度 L=30 m；膨脹係數 alpha=1.2e-05 1/K；溫度變化 dT=20 K。公式 y=L*alpha*dT*1000，代入得 y=7.2 mm。邊界：均勻溫度與自由伸長；不包含熱梯度引起的彎曲。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: member length L=30 m; expansion coefficient alpha=1.2e-05 1/K; temperature change dT=20 K. Formula y=L*alpha*dT*1000 gives y=7.2 mm. Boundary: Uniform temperature and free expansion; thermal-gradient bending is omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多點溫度檢查均勻假設，再對照端點位移與支承狀態，分辨自由與拘束行為。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check temperature uniformity at several points and compare end movement with support condition to distinguish free and restrained behaviour.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：構件長度 L=30 m；膨脹係數 alpha=1.2e-05 1/K；溫度變化 dT=20 K。公式 y=L*alpha*dT*1000，代入得 y=7.2 mm。邊界：均勻溫度與自由伸長；不包含熱梯度引起的彎曲。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: member length L=30 m; expansion coefficient alpha=1.2e-05 1/K; temperature change dT=20 K. Formula y=L*alpha*dT*1000 gives y=7.2 mm. Boundary: Uniform temperature and free expansion; thermal-gradient bending is omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal movement and support travel\", which statement holds?","options":["幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣","三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限","原創假想教學輸入：構件長度 L=30 m；膨脹係數 alpha=1.2e-05 1/K；溫度變化 dT=20 K。"],"optionsEn":["Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength.","Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: member length L=30 m; expansion coefficient alpha=1.2e-05 1/K; temperature change dT=20 K."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：構件長度 L=30 m；膨脹係數 alpha=1.2e-05 1/K；溫度變化 dT=20 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: member length L=30 m; expansion coefficient alpha=1.2e-05 1/K; temperature change dT=20 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b397-v16-15","title":"導梁伸縮與支承活動：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal movement and support travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導梁伸縮與支承活動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal movement and support travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多點溫度檢查均勻假設，再對照端點位移與支承狀態，分辨自由與拘束行為。以「導梁伸縮與支承活動」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check temperature uniformity at several points and compare end movement with support condition to distinguish free and restrained behaviour. For thermal movement and support travel, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把構件長度 L 從 30 改成 33 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 7.2 變為 7.92 mm。先說明「導梁伸縮與支承活動」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only member length L from 30 to 33 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 7.2 to 7.92 mm. Explain the causal direction for thermal movement and support travel, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：支承卡住可能讓位移很小但內力增加，日照溫差又可能造成彎曲而非單純伸長。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A seized support can suppress movement while increasing force; solar gradients may cause bending rather than simple extension. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多點溫度檢查均勻假設，再對照端點位移與支承狀態，分辨自由與拘束行為。以「導梁伸縮與支承活動」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Check temperature uniformity at several points and compare end movement with support condition to distinguish free and restrained behaviour. For thermal movement and support travel, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把構件長度 L 從 30 改成 33 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 7.2 變為 7.92 mm。先說明「導梁伸縮與支承活動」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only member length L from 30 to 33 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 7.2 to 7.92 mm. Explain the causal direction for thermal movement and support travel, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導梁伸縮與支承活動」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal movement and support travel\"?","options":["以多點溫度檢查均勻假設，再對照端點位移與支承狀態，分辨自由與拘束行為。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍"],"optionsEn":["Check temperature uniformity at several points and compare end movement with support condition to distinguish free and restrained behaviour.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以多點溫度檢查均勻假設，再對照端點位移與支承狀態，分辨自由與拘束行為。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check temperature uniformity at several points and compare end movement with support condition to distinguish free and restrained behaviour. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b397-v16-16","title":"導梁伸縮與支承活動：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal movement and support travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal movement and support travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承卡住可能讓位移很小但內力增加，日照溫差又可能造成彎曲而非單純伸長。回到「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A seized support can suppress movement while increasing force; solar gradients may cause bending rather than simple extension. Trace the input chain for thermal movement and support travel. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻溫度與自由伸長；不包含熱梯度引起的彎曲。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform temperature and free expansion; thermal-gradient bending is omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承卡住可能讓位移很小但內力增加，日照溫差又可能造成彎曲而非單純伸長。回到「導梁伸縮與支承活動」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"A seized support can suppress movement while increasing force; solar gradients may cause bending rather than simple extension. Trace the input chain for thermal movement and support travel. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導梁伸縮與支承活動」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal movement and support travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","支承卡住可能讓位移很小但內力增加，日照溫差又可能造成彎曲而非單純伸長。","同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A seized support can suppress movement while increasing force; solar gradients may cause bending rather than simple extension.","Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承卡住可能讓位移很小但內力增加，日照溫差又可能造成彎曲而非單純伸長。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A seized support can suppress movement while increasing force; solar gradients may cause bending rather than simple extension. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b397-v16-s3","title":"導向面幾何控制網與幾何量測隨機成分","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces & Random components of geometry measurement","description":"本階段聚焦「導向面幾何控制網」與「幾何量測隨機成分」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Survey control for guide surfaces\" and \"Random components of geometry measurement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b397-v16-17","title":"導向面幾何控制網：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「導向面幾何控制網」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Survey control for guide surfaces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"車輛接觸的導向面必須與控制網建立可重複的幾何關係，長視線會放大角度誤差。以閉合觀測檢查基準一致性，不用單站重複性代替全線準確度。小角度方向誤差會隨視線距離放大成橫向位置誤差，長視線不一定帶來更準的幾何控制。基準網、折光、儀器對中與目標安裝都會影響結果；同一站多次讀值一致，仍可能共同受到基準偏移影響。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：小角近似與單一方向誤差，未含完整測量網平差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導向面幾何控制網」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tie contact guide surfaces reproducibly to the control network because angular error grows with sight distance. Use closure checks rather than substituting repeated readings at one station for network accuracy. A small angular error becomes transverse position error proportional to sight distance, so a longer sight is not automatically more accurate. Control networks, refraction, centring and target mounting all matter. Repeated agreement from one station can still share a common datum error. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Small-angle approximation for one direction error, not a complete survey-network adjustment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Survey control for guide surfaces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：視線距離 distance=40 m；小角誤差 angle=2.5e-05 rad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sight distance distance=40 m; small angular error angle=2.5e-05 rad.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導向面幾何控制網」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Survey control for guide surfaces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-17-k1","title":"導向面幾何控制網","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces","text":"車輛接觸的導向面必須與控制網建立可重複的幾何關係，長視線會放大角度誤差。以閉合觀測檢查基準一致性，不用單站重複性代替全線準確度。","textEn":"Tie contact guide surfaces reproducibly to the control network because angular error grows with sight distance. Use closure checks rather than substituting repeated readings at one station for network accuracy.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導向面幾何控制網」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Survey control for guide surfaces\" is correct?","options":["同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確","任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","車輛接觸的導向面必須與控制網建立可重複的幾何關係，長視線會放大角度誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position.","Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Tie contact guide surfaces reproducibly to the control network because angular error grows with sight distance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"車輛接觸的導向面必須與控制網建立可重複的幾何關係，長視線會放大角度誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tie contact guide surfaces reproducibly to the control network because angular error grows with sight distance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b397-v16-18","title":"導向面幾何控制網：定量估算","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導向面幾何控制網」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Survey control for guide surfaces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：視線距離 distance=40 m；小角誤差 angle=2.5e-05 rad。公式 y=distance*angle*1000，代入得 y=1 mm。邊界：小角近似與單一方向誤差，未含完整測量網平差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sight distance distance=40 m; small angular error angle=2.5e-05 rad. Formula y=distance*angle*1000 gives y=1 mm. Boundary: Small-angle approximation for one direction error, not a complete survey-network adjustment. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用不同站位與往返觀測交叉核對，將角度誤差、對中誤差與基準移動分列。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check from different stations and reciprocal observations, separating angular error, centring and datum movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：視線距離 distance=40 m；小角誤差 angle=2.5e-05 rad。公式 y=distance*angle*1000，代入得 y=1 mm。邊界：小角近似與單一方向誤差，未含完整測量網平差。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sight distance distance=40 m; small angular error angle=2.5e-05 rad. Formula y=distance*angle*1000 gives y=1 mm. Boundary: Small-angle approximation for one direction error, not a complete survey-network adjustment.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導向面幾何控制網」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Survey control for guide surfaces\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：視線距離 distance=40 m；小角誤差 angle=2.5e-05 rad。","結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sight distance distance=40 m; small angular error angle=2.5e-05 rad.","A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：視線距離 distance=40 m；小角誤差 angle=2.5e-05 rad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sight distance distance=40 m; small angular error angle=2.5e-05 rad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b397-v16-19","title":"導向面幾何控制網：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導向面幾何控制網」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Survey control for guide surfaces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用不同站位與往返觀測交叉核對，將角度誤差、對中誤差與基準移動分列。以「導向面幾何控制網」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check from different stations and reciprocal observations, separating angular error, centring and datum movement. For survey control for guide surfaces, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把視線距離 distance 從 40 改成 44 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1 變為 1.1 mm。先說明「導向面幾何控制網」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only sight distance distance from 40 to 44 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1 to 1.1 mm. Explain the causal direction for survey control for guide surfaces, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器重複性良好可能掩蓋穩定的對中偏差，熱折光則使日夜結果有系統差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Good repeatability can conceal stable centring bias; thermal refraction can create systematic day-night differences. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用不同站位與往返觀測交叉核對，將角度誤差、對中誤差與基準移動分列。以「導向面幾何控制網」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Cross-check from different stations and reciprocal observations, separating angular error, centring and datum movement. For survey control for guide surfaces, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把視線距離 distance 從 40 改成 44 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1 變為 1.1 mm。先說明「導向面幾何控制網」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only sight distance distance from 40 to 44 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1 to 1.1 mm. Explain the causal direction for survey control for guide surfaces, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導向面幾何控制網」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Survey control for guide surfaces\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用不同站位與往返觀測交叉核對，將角度誤差、對中誤差與基準移動分列。","導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Cross-check from different stations and reciprocal observations, separating angular error, centring and datum movement.","Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用不同站位與往返觀測交叉核對，將角度誤差、對中誤差與基準移動分列。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check from different stations and reciprocal observations, separating angular error, centring and datum movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b397-v16-20","title":"導向面幾何控制網：失效診斷","titleEn":"Survey control for guide surfaces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導向面幾何控制網」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Survey control for guide surfaces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器重複性良好可能掩蓋穩定的對中偏差，熱折光則使日夜結果有系統差異。回到「導向面幾何控制網」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Good repeatability can conceal stable centring bias; thermal refraction can create systematic day-night differences. Trace the input chain for survey control for guide surfaces. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：小角近似與單一方向誤差，未含完整測量網平差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Small-angle approximation for one direction error, not a complete survey-network adjustment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器重複性良好可能掩蓋穩定的對中偏差，熱折光則使日夜結果有系統差異。回到「導向面幾何控制網」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Good repeatability can conceal stable centring bias; thermal refraction can create systematic day-night differences. Trace the input chain for survey control for guide surfaces. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導向面幾何控制網」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Survey control for guide surfaces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","儀器重複性良好可能掩蓋穩定的對中偏差，熱折光則使日夜結果有系統差異。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Good repeatability can conceal stable centring bias; thermal refraction can create systematic day-night differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"儀器重複性良好可能掩蓋穩定的對中偏差，熱折光則使日夜結果有系統差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Good repeatability can conceal stable centring bias; thermal refraction can create systematic day-night differences. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b397-v16-21","title":"幾何量測隨機成分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Random components of geometry measurement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「幾何量測隨機成分」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Random components of geometry measurement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將獨立儀器讀值的標準差與共同基準偏差分開，再決定能否平方和合成。若左右導向面共用同一基準，必須保留相關性而非盲目縮小誤差。獨立零均值誤差的變異數可以相加，因此標準差以平方和開根號合成。這個做法不適合直接合併最大容差或共同偏差；一旦共享基準造成相關性，協方差項就必須回到計算中，不能繼續假裝量測彼此獨立。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立隨機標準差，不代表確定的最大偏移界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「幾何量測隨機成分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate independent-reading standard deviations from common datum bias before root-sum-square combination. Retain correlations when both guide surfaces share a reference rather than automatically shrinking the uncertainty. Variances of independent zero-mean errors add, giving a root-sum-square standard deviation. This is not a way to combine maximum tolerances or common bias. When a shared datum creates correlation, covariance terms belong in the calculation rather than assuming continued independence. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent random standard deviations, not a deterministic maximum displacement bound. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Random components of geometry measurement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立誤差一標準差 s1=3 mm；獨立誤差二標準差 s2=4 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: first independent standard deviation s1=3 mm; second independent standard deviation s2=4 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「幾何量測隨機成分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Random components of geometry measurement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-21-k1","title":"幾何量測隨機成分","titleEn":"Random components of geometry measurement","text":"將獨立儀器讀值的標準差與共同基準偏差分開，再決定能否平方和合成。若左右導向面共用同一基準，必須保留相關性而非盲目縮小誤差。","textEn":"Separate independent-reading standard deviations from common datum bias before root-sum-square combination. Retain correlations when both guide surfaces share a reference rather than automatically shrinking the uncertainty.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「幾何量測隨機成分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Random components of geometry measurement\" is correct?","options":["將獨立儀器讀值的標準差與共同基準偏差分開，再決定能否平方和合成。","任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣"],"optionsEn":["Separate independent-reading standard deviations from common datum bias before root-sum-square combination.","Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將獨立儀器讀值的標準差與共同基準偏差分開，再決定能否平方和合成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate independent-reading standard deviations from common datum bias before root-sum-square combination. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b397-v16-22","title":"幾何量測隨機成分：定量估算","titleEn":"Random components of geometry measurement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「幾何量測隨機成分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Random components of geometry measurement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立誤差一標準差 s1=3 mm；獨立誤差二標準差 s2=4 mm。公式 y=sqrt(s1*s1+s2*s2)，代入得 y=5 mm。邊界：獨立隨機標準差，不代表確定的最大偏移界。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: first independent standard deviation s1=3 mm; second independent standard deviation s2=4 mm. Formula y=sqrt(s1*s1+s2*s2) gives y=5 mm. Boundary: Independent random standard deviations, not a deterministic maximum displacement bound. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以重複量測估計標準差與相關係數，將固定偏差另列，再核對合成殘差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate standard deviations and correlation from repeated observations, separate fixed bias, and compare combined residuals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立誤差一標準差 s1=3 mm；獨立誤差二標準差 s2=4 mm。公式 y=sqrt(s1*s1+s2*s2)，代入得 y=5 mm。邊界：獨立隨機標準差，不代表確定的最大偏移界。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: first independent standard deviation s1=3 mm; second independent standard deviation s2=4 mm. Formula y=sqrt(s1*s1+s2*s2) gives y=5 mm. Boundary: Independent random standard deviations, not a deterministic maximum displacement bound.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「幾何量測隨機成分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Random components of geometry measurement\", which statement holds?","options":["三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限","原創假想教學輸入：獨立誤差一標準差 s1=3 mm；獨立誤差二標準差 s2=4 mm。","跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍"],"optionsEn":["Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: first independent standard deviation s1=3 mm; second independent standard deviation s2=4 mm.","Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立誤差一標準差 s1=3 mm；獨立誤差二標準差 s2=4 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: first independent standard deviation s1=3 mm; second independent standard deviation s2=4 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b397-v16-23","title":"幾何量測隨機成分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Random components of geometry measurement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「幾何量測隨機成分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Random components of geometry measurement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以重複量測估計標準差與相關係數，將固定偏差另列，再核對合成殘差。以「幾何量測隨機成分」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate standard deviations and correlation from repeated observations, separate fixed bias, and compare combined residuals. For random components of geometry measurement, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把獨立誤差一標準差 s1 從 3 改成 3.3 mm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 5 變為 5.18556 mm。先說明「幾何量測隨機成分」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only first independent standard deviation s1 from 3 to 3.3 mm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 5 to 5.18556 mm. Explain the causal direction for random components of geometry measurement, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：共同基準誤差會使所有讀值同向偏移，重複次數增加也無法把這種偏差平均掉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A common datum error shifts readings together, and additional repetition cannot average away that shared bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以重複量測估計標準差與相關係數，將固定偏差另列，再核對合成殘差。以「幾何量測隨機成分」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Estimate standard deviations and correlation from repeated observations, separate fixed bias, and compare combined residuals. For random components of geometry measurement, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把獨立誤差一標準差 s1 從 3 改成 3.3 mm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 5 變為 5.18556 mm。先說明「幾何量測隨機成分」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only first independent standard deviation s1 from 3 to 3.3 mm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 5 to 5.18556 mm. Explain the causal direction for random components of geometry measurement, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「幾何量測隨機成分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Random components of geometry measurement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍","以重複量測估計標準差與相關係數，將固定偏差另列，再核對合成殘差。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.","Estimate standard deviations and correlation from repeated observations, separate fixed bias, and compare combined residuals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以重複量測估計標準差與相關係數，將固定偏差另列，再核對合成殘差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate standard deviations and correlation from repeated observations, separate fixed bias, and compare combined residuals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b397-v16-24","title":"幾何量測隨機成分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Random components of geometry measurement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「幾何量測隨機成分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Random components of geometry measurement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共同基準誤差會使所有讀值同向偏移，重複次數增加也無法把這種偏差平均掉。回到「幾何量測隨機成分」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A common datum error shifts readings together, and additional repetition cannot average away that shared bias. Trace the input chain for random components of geometry measurement. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立隨機標準差，不代表確定的最大偏移界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent random standard deviations, not a deterministic maximum displacement bound.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共同基準誤差會使所有讀值同向偏移，重複次數增加也無法把這種偏差平均掉。回到「幾何量測隨機成分」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"A common datum error shifts readings together, and additional repetition cannot average away that shared bias. Trace the input chain for random components of geometry measurement. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「幾何量測隨機成分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Random components of geometry measurement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共同基準誤差會使所有讀值同向偏移，重複次數增加也無法把這種偏差平均掉。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣"],"optionsEn":["A common datum error shifts readings together, and additional repetition cannot average away that shared bias.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共同基準誤差會使所有讀值同向偏移，重複次數增加也無法把這種偏差平均掉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A common datum error shifts readings together, and additional repetition cannot average away that shared bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b397-v16-s4","title":"導梁波長與行車激振與剛度質量與模態概念","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation & Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation","description":"本階段聚焦「導梁波長與行車激振」與「剛度質量與模態概念」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Guideway wavelength and running excitation\" and \"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b397-v16-25","title":"導梁波長與行車激振：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「導梁波長與行車激振」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Guideway wavelength and running excitation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相同幾何波長在不同車速下形成不同時間頻率，因此只看最大偏差會漏掉動態資訊。將量測波長與車速並列，找出需要車輛模型進一步分析的組合。固定空間波長在移動車輛上轉換成時間激振頻率，因此同一幾何不平順在不同速度下可能接近不同振動模態。只看最大偏差會漏掉波長資訊；導梁精度控制需要把幾何頻譜、車速與車輛動態連結，而非只追求單點誤差最小。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定速通過單一正弦空間成分，未計車輛傳遞函數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導梁波長與行車激振」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The same geometric wavelength produces different temporal frequencies at different speeds, so peak deviation alone misses dynamic information. Pair wavelength with speed to identify combinations needing a vehicle-response model. A spatial wavelength becomes a temporal excitation frequency on a moving vehicle, so the same geometry can excite different modes at different speeds. Maximum deviation alone loses wavelength information. Guideway precision therefore links geometry spectra, speed and vehicle dynamics rather than only minimizing point errors. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-speed passage over one sinusoidal spatial component; the vehicle transfer function is not included. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Guideway wavelength and running excitation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：運行速度 speed=40 m/s；幾何波長 wavelength=20 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: running speed speed=40 m/s; geometric wavelength wavelength=20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導梁波長與行車激振」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Guideway wavelength and running excitation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-25-k1","title":"導梁波長與行車激振","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation","text":"相同幾何波長在不同車速下形成不同時間頻率，因此只看最大偏差會漏掉動態資訊。將量測波長與車速並列，找出需要車輛模型進一步分析的組合。","textEn":"The same geometric wavelength produces different temporal frequencies at different speeds, so peak deviation alone misses dynamic information. Pair wavelength with speed to identify combinations needing a vehicle-response model.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導梁波長與行車激振」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Guideway wavelength and running excitation\" is correct?","options":["幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣","相同幾何波長在不同車速下形成不同時間頻率，因此只看最大偏差會漏掉動態資訊。","結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小"],"optionsEn":["Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength.","The same geometric wavelength produces different temporal frequencies at different speeds, so peak deviation alone misses dynamic information.","A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同幾何波長在不同車速下形成不同時間頻率，因此只看最大偏差會漏掉動態資訊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The same geometric wavelength produces different temporal frequencies at different speeds, so peak deviation alone misses dynamic information. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b397-v16-26","title":"導梁波長與行車激振：定量估算","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導梁波長與行車激振」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Guideway wavelength and running excitation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：運行速度 speed=40 m/s；幾何波長 wavelength=20 m。公式 y=speed/wavelength，代入得 y=2 Hz。邊界：定速通過單一正弦空間成分，未計車輛傳遞函數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: running speed speed=40 m/s; geometric wavelength wavelength=20 m. Formula y=speed/wavelength gives y=2 Hz. Boundary: Constant-speed passage over one sinusoidal spatial component; the vehicle transfer function is not included. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將幾何資料按里程頻譜分析，再用速度轉換頻率，與車上加速度頻譜比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Analyse geometry by spatial frequency, transform using speed, and compare with onboard acceleration spectra.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：運行速度 speed=40 m/s；幾何波長 wavelength=20 m。公式 y=speed/wavelength，代入得 y=2 Hz。邊界：定速通過單一正弦空間成分，未計車輛傳遞函數。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: running speed speed=40 m/s; geometric wavelength wavelength=20 m. Formula y=speed/wavelength gives y=2 Hz. Boundary: Constant-speed passage over one sinusoidal spatial component; the vehicle transfer function is not included.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導梁波長與行車激振」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Guideway wavelength and running excitation\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉","原創假想教學輸入：運行速度 speed=40 m/s；幾何波長 wavelength=20 m。"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: running speed speed=40 m/s; geometric wavelength wavelength=20 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：運行速度 speed=40 m/s；幾何波長 wavelength=20 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: running speed speed=40 m/s; geometric wavelength wavelength=20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b397-v16-27","title":"導梁波長與行車激振：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導梁波長與行車激振」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Guideway wavelength and running excitation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將幾何資料按里程頻譜分析，再用速度轉換頻率，與車上加速度頻譜比較。以「導梁波長與行車激振」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Analyse geometry by spatial frequency, transform using speed, and compare with onboard acceleration spectra. For guideway wavelength and running excitation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把運行速度 speed 從 40 改成 44 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2 變為 2.2 Hz。先說明「導梁波長與行車激振」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only running speed speed from 40 to 44 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2 to 2.2 Hz. Explain the causal direction for guideway wavelength and running excitation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：里程軸不均勻會扭曲頻譜，忽略車輛模態又可能把所有波長視為同樣重要。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven distance sampling distorts spectra; ignoring vehicle modes incorrectly treats every wavelength as equally important. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將幾何資料按里程頻譜分析，再用速度轉換頻率，與車上加速度頻譜比較。以「導梁波長與行車激振」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Analyse geometry by spatial frequency, transform using speed, and compare with onboard acceleration spectra. For guideway wavelength and running excitation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把運行速度 speed 從 40 改成 44 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2 變為 2.2 Hz。先說明「導梁波長與行車激振」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only running speed speed from 40 to 44 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2 to 2.2 Hz. Explain the causal direction for guideway wavelength and running excitation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導梁波長與行車激振」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Guideway wavelength and running excitation\"?","options":["將幾何資料按里程頻譜分析，再用速度轉換頻率，與車上加速度頻譜比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Analyse geometry by spatial frequency, transform using speed, and compare with onboard acceleration spectra.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將幾何資料按里程頻譜分析，再用速度轉換頻率，與車上加速度頻譜比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Analyse geometry by spatial frequency, transform using speed, and compare with onboard acceleration spectra. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b397-v16-28","title":"導梁波長與行車激振：失效診斷","titleEn":"Guideway wavelength and running excitation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導梁波長與行車激振」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Guideway wavelength and running excitation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"里程軸不均勻會扭曲頻譜，忽略車輛模態又可能把所有波長視為同樣重要。回到「導梁波長與行車激振」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven distance sampling distorts spectra; ignoring vehicle modes incorrectly treats every wavelength as equally important. Trace the input chain for guideway wavelength and running excitation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定速通過單一正弦空間成分，未計車輛傳遞函數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-speed passage over one sinusoidal spatial component; the vehicle transfer function is not included.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"里程軸不均勻會扭曲頻譜，忽略車輛模態又可能把所有波長視為同樣重要。回到「導梁波長與行車激振」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Uneven distance sampling distorts spectra; ignoring vehicle modes incorrectly treats every wavelength as equally important. Trace the input chain for guideway wavelength and running excitation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導梁波長與行車激振」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Guideway wavelength and running excitation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","里程軸不均勻會扭曲頻譜，忽略車輛模態又可能把所有波長視為同樣重要。","結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Uneven distance sampling distorts spectra; ignoring vehicle modes incorrectly treats every wavelength as equally important.","A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"里程軸不均勻會扭曲頻譜，忽略車輛模態又可能把所有波長視為同樣重要。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven distance sampling distorts spectra; ignoring vehicle modes incorrectly treats every wavelength as equally important. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b397-v16-29","title":"剛度質量與模態概念：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「剛度質量與模態概念」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"先用單自由度模型理解剛度和質量如何改變固有頻率，再比較來自導梁幾何的激振。模型沒有阻尼與多模態，不能只憑頻率相近就估計真實放大量。單自由度固有頻率由剛度與質量比的平方根決定。提高剛度可能移開一個激振頻率，也可能移近另一個頻率；阻尼控制峰值而不只改變頻率，因此僅比較靜態變形不能預測動態放大。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：線性無阻尼單自由度頻率，未含多模態與輪軌或磁路耦合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剛度質量與模態概念」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use one degree of freedom to understand stiffness and mass effects before comparing guideway excitation. With damping and multiple modes absent, frequency proximity alone cannot determine actual amplification. A single-degree natural frequency follows the square root of stiffness-to-mass ratio. Stiffening can move away from one excitation yet toward another. Damping controls the resonant peak as well as frequency effects, so static deflection alone cannot predict dynamic amplification. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear undamped single-degree frequency without multimode, wheel-rail or magnetic coupling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：等效剛度 k=1.8e+06 N/m；等效質量 m=12000 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent stiffness k=1.8e+06 N/m; equivalent mass m=12000 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剛度質量與模態概念」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-29-k1","title":"剛度質量與模態概念","titleEn":"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation","text":"先用單自由度模型理解剛度和質量如何改變固有頻率，再比較來自導梁幾何的激振。模型沒有阻尼與多模態，不能只憑頻率相近就估計真實放大量。","textEn":"Use one degree of freedom to understand stiffness and mass effects before comparing guideway excitation. With damping and multiple modes absent, frequency proximity alone cannot determine actual amplification.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剛度質量與模態概念」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation\" is correct?","options":["結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小","三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限","先用單自由度模型理解剛度和質量如何改變固有頻率，再比較來自導梁幾何的激振。"],"optionsEn":["A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed.","Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.","Use one degree of freedom to understand stiffness and mass effects before comparing guideway excitation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先用單自由度模型理解剛度和質量如何改變固有頻率，再比較來自導梁幾何的激振。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use one degree of freedom to understand stiffness and mass effects before comparing guideway excitation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b397-v16-30","title":"剛度質量與模態概念：定量估算","titleEn":"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剛度質量與模態概念」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：等效剛度 k=1.8e+06 N/m；等效質量 m=12000 kg。公式 y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)，代入得 y=1.94924 Hz。邊界：線性無阻尼單自由度頻率，未含多模態與輪軌或磁路耦合。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent stiffness k=1.8e+06 N/m; equivalent mass m=12000 kg. Formula y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi) gives y=1.94924 Hz. Boundary: Linear undamped single-degree frequency without multimode, wheel-rail or magnetic coupling. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用低能量掃頻或自由衰減試驗量頻率與阻尼，對照載重改變後的模態移動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure frequency and damping with low-energy sweep or free decay, then compare modal shifts after changing load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：等效剛度 k=1.8e+06 N/m；等效質量 m=12000 kg。公式 y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)，代入得 y=1.94924 Hz。邊界：線性無阻尼單自由度頻率，未含多模態與輪軌或磁路耦合。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent stiffness k=1.8e+06 N/m; equivalent mass m=12000 kg. Formula y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi) gives y=1.94924 Hz. Boundary: Linear undamped single-degree frequency without multimode, wheel-rail or magnetic coupling.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剛度質量與模態概念」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：等效剛度 k=1.8e+06 N/m；等效質量 m=12000 kg。","跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍","速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent stiffness k=1.8e+06 N/m; equivalent mass m=12000 kg.","Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection.","Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：等效剛度 k=1.8e+06 N/m；等效質量 m=12000 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent stiffness k=1.8e+06 N/m; equivalent mass m=12000 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b397-v16-31","title":"剛度質量與模態概念：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剛度質量與模態概念」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用低能量掃頻或自由衰減試驗量頻率與阻尼，對照載重改變後的模態移動。以「剛度質量與模態概念」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure frequency and damping with low-energy sweep or free decay, then compare modal shifts after changing load. For stiffness, mass and modal interpretation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把等效剛度 k 從 1.8e+06 改成 1.98e+06 N/m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.94924 變為 2.04438 Hz。先說明「剛度質量與模態概念」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only equivalent stiffness k from 1.8e+06 to 1.98e+06 N/m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.94924 to 2.04438 Hz. Explain the causal direction for stiffness, mass and modal interpretation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只增加剛度而忽略激振頻帶可能使振動更大，感測器裝在節點則可能漏掉主要模態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stiffening without considering excitation bands can increase vibration; a sensor at a node may miss the dominant mode. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用低能量掃頻或自由衰減試驗量頻率與阻尼，對照載重改變後的模態移動。以「剛度質量與模態概念」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure frequency and damping with low-energy sweep or free decay, then compare modal shifts after changing load. For stiffness, mass and modal interpretation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把等效剛度 k 從 1.8e+06 改成 1.98e+06 N/m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.94924 變為 2.04438 Hz。先說明「剛度質量與模態概念」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only equivalent stiffness k from 1.8e+06 to 1.98e+06 N/m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.94924 to 2.04438 Hz. Explain the causal direction for stiffness, mass and modal interpretation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剛度質量與模態概念」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用低能量掃頻或自由衰減試驗量頻率與阻尼，對照載重改變後的模態移動。","同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Measure frequency and damping with low-energy sweep or free decay, then compare modal shifts after changing load.","Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用低能量掃頻或自由衰減試驗量頻率與阻尼，對照載重改變後的模態移動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure frequency and damping with low-energy sweep or free decay, then compare modal shifts after changing load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b397-v16-32","title":"剛度質量與模態概念：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剛度質量與模態概念」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只增加剛度而忽略激振頻帶可能使振動更大，感測器裝在節點則可能漏掉主要模態。回到「剛度質量與模態概念」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stiffening without considering excitation bands can increase vibration; a sensor at a node may miss the dominant mode. Trace the input chain for stiffness, mass and modal interpretation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：線性無阻尼單自由度頻率，未含多模態與輪軌或磁路耦合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear undamped single-degree frequency without multimode, wheel-rail or magnetic coupling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「結構越硬就能保證任何速度下振動都一定更小」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A stiffer structure always guarantees smaller vibration at every speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只增加剛度而忽略激振頻帶可能使振動更大，感測器裝在節點則可能漏掉主要模態。回到「剛度質量與模態概念」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Stiffening without considering excitation bands can increase vibration; a sensor at a node may miss the dominant mode. Trace the input chain for stiffness, mass and modal interpretation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛度質量與模態概念」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stiffness, mass and modal interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限","只增加剛度而忽略激振頻帶可能使振動更大，感測器裝在節點則可能漏掉主要模態。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.","Stiffening without considering excitation bands can increase vibration; a sensor at a node may miss the dominant mode."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只增加剛度而忽略激振頻帶可能使振動更大，感測器裝在節點則可能漏掉主要模態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stiffening without considering excitation bands can increase vibration; a sensor at a node may miss the dominant mode. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b397-v16-s5","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面與彎扭溫度整合案例","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface & Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases","description":"本階段聚焦「導梁車輛與月台界面」與「彎扭溫度整合案例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface\" and \"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b397-v16-33","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「導梁車輛與月台界面」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將導梁位置、懸吊移動和月台測量放到同一間隙預算，避免土建與車輛各自合格卻介面衝突。明確區分有界容差與隨機標準差，不能互換合成方法。月台與車體介面的間隙預算需分開列入軌道幾何、懸吊移動與測量誤差。保守界限可直接相加，而隨機誤差合成必須有分布與相關性證據；只在空車靜止狀態量一個間隙，無法代表載重與動態情境。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：三項同向有界誤差的保守和，不是法定間隙允收值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導梁車輛與月台界面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Combine guideway position, suspension movement and platform survey in one gap budget to expose interface conflicts between separately acceptable disciplines. Distinguish bounded tolerances from random standard deviations when combining them. A platform-vehicle gap budget separates track geometry, suspension movement and survey error. Conservative bounds can be summed, while stochastic combination requires evidence for distributions and correlation. One stationary empty-vehicle measurement cannot represent loaded and dynamic conditions. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Conservative sum of three same-direction bounded errors, not a statutory gap allowance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：軌道偏移界 track=8 mm；車體位移界 body=10 mm；測量誤差界 survey=3 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: track offset bound track=8 mm; body displacement bound body=10 mm; survey error bound survey=3 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導梁車輛與月台界面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-33-k1","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface","text":"將導梁位置、懸吊移動和月台測量放到同一間隙預算，避免土建與車輛各自合格卻介面衝突。明確區分有界容差與隨機標準差，不能互換合成方法。","textEn":"Combine guideway position, suspension movement and platform survey in one gap budget to expose interface conflicts between separately acceptable disciplines. Distinguish bounded tolerances from random standard deviations when combining them.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導梁車輛與月台界面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface\" is correct?","options":["將導梁位置、懸吊移動和月台測量放到同一間隙預算，避免土建與車輛各自合格卻介面衝突。","三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Combine guideway position, suspension movement and platform survey in one gap budget to expose interface conflicts between separately acceptable disciplines.","Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將導梁位置、懸吊移動和月台測量放到同一間隙預算，避免土建與車輛各自合格卻介面衝突。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Combine guideway position, suspension movement and platform survey in one gap budget to expose interface conflicts between separately acceptable disciplines. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b397-v16-34","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面：定量估算","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導梁車輛與月台界面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：軌道偏移界 track=8 mm；車體位移界 body=10 mm；測量誤差界 survey=3 mm。公式 y=track+body+survey，代入得 y=21 mm。邊界：三項同向有界誤差的保守和，不是法定間隙允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: track offset bound track=8 mm; body displacement bound body=10 mm; survey error bound survey=3 mm. Formula y=track+body+survey gives y=21 mm. Boundary: Conservative sum of three same-direction bounded errors, not a statutory gap allowance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立共同座標，對空載、載重及不同車型分別量測，並保留各誤差來源的符號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish one coordinate system, measure empty and loaded vehicles of each type, and retain signs of individual error sources.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：軌道偏移界 track=8 mm；車體位移界 body=10 mm；測量誤差界 survey=3 mm。公式 y=track+body+survey，代入得 y=21 mm。邊界：三項同向有界誤差的保守和，不是法定間隙允收值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: track offset bound track=8 mm; body displacement bound body=10 mm; survey error bound survey=3 mm. Formula y=track+body+survey gives y=21 mm. Boundary: Conservative sum of three same-direction bounded errors, not a statutory gap allowance.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導梁車輛與月台界面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface\", which statement holds?","options":["導梁中心線沒有明顯下沉就表示不可能發生扭轉","原創假想教學輸入：軌道偏移界 track=8 mm；車體位移界 body=10 mm；測量誤差界 survey=3 mm。","量不到熱伸長就表示構件完全沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Little guideway-centreline settlement proves that torsion cannot occur.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: track offset bound track=8 mm; body displacement bound body=10 mm; survey error bound survey=3 mm.","No measured thermal expansion means that a member has no thermal stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：軌道偏移界 track=8 mm；車體位移界 body=10 mm；測量誤差界 survey=3 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: track offset bound track=8 mm; body displacement bound body=10 mm; survey error bound survey=3 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b397-v16-35","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導梁車輛與月台界面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立共同座標，對空載、載重及不同車型分別量測，並保留各誤差來源的符號。以「導梁車輛與月台界面」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish one coordinate system, measure empty and loaded vehicles of each type, and retain signs of individual error sources. For guideway, vehicle and platform interface, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把車體位移界 body 從 10 改成 11 mm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 21 變為 22 mm。先說明「導梁車輛與月台界面」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only body displacement bound body from 10 to 11 mm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 21 to 22 mm. Explain the causal direction for guideway, vehicle and platform interface, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把最大值當成標準差再作均方根合成會失去保守性，基準點沉陷也會造成整排讀值偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating maxima as standard deviations and applying root-sum-square loses conservatism; datum settlement can bias the whole measurement row. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立共同座標，對空載、載重及不同車型分別量測，並保留各誤差來源的符號。以「導梁車輛與月台界面」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Establish one coordinate system, measure empty and loaded vehicles of each type, and retain signs of individual error sources. For guideway, vehicle and platform interface, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把車體位移界 body 從 10 改成 11 mm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 21 變為 22 mm。先說明「導梁車輛與月台界面」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only body displacement bound body from 10 to 11 mm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 21 to 22 mm. Explain the causal direction for guideway, vehicle and platform interface, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導梁車輛與月台界面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","任何兩個誤差都可以不問相關性直接平方和開根號","建立共同座標，對空載、載重及不同車型分別量測，並保留各誤差來源的符號。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Any two errors can be combined by root-sum-square without considering correlation.","Establish one coordinate system, measure empty and loaded vehicles of each type, and retain signs of individual error sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立共同座標，對空載、載重及不同車型分別量測，並保留各誤差來源的符號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish one coordinate system, measure empty and loaded vehicles of each type, and retain signs of individual error sources. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b397-v16-36","title":"導梁車輛與月台界面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導梁車輛與月台界面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Guideway, vehicle and platform interface” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把最大值當成標準差再作均方根合成會失去保守性，基準點沉陷也會造成整排讀值偏移。回到「導梁車輛與月台界面」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating maxima as standard deviations and applying root-sum-square loses conservatism; datum settlement can bias the whole measurement row. Trace the input chain for guideway, vehicle and platform interface. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：三項同向有界誤差的保守和，不是法定間隙允收值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Conservative sum of three same-direction bounded errors, not a statutory gap allowance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「三個最大誤差都可直接用均方根方式縮小總界限」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Three maximum error bounds may always be reduced through root-sum-square combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把最大值當成標準差再作均方根合成會失去保守性，基準點沉陷也會造成整排讀值偏移。回到「導梁車輛與月台界面」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Treating maxima as standard deviations and applying root-sum-square loses conservatism; datum settlement can bias the whole measurement row. Trace the input chain for guideway, vehicle and platform interface. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導梁車輛與月台界面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Guideway, vehicle and platform interface\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把最大值當成標準差再作均方根合成會失去保守性，基準點沉陷也會造成整排讀值偏移。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Treating maxima as standard deviations and applying root-sum-square loses conservatism; datum settlement can bias the whole measurement row.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把最大值當成標準差再作均方根合成會失去保守性，基準點沉陷也會造成整排讀值偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating maxima as standard deviations and applying root-sum-square loses conservatism; datum settlement can bias the whole measurement row. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b397-v16-37","title":"彎扭溫度整合案例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「彎扭溫度整合案例」如何影響跨座式單軌導梁的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Straddle-monorail guideway beams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把載重位置、溫度條件與支承狀態分成可追溯案例，確認檢測不只涵蓋正中靜載。保留各模型未處理的耦合項，交付時指出仍需更完整分析的邊界。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彎扭溫度整合案例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trace load location, temperature and support state through cases that extend beyond centred static loading. Retain omitted coupling mechanisms and identify boundaries requiring fuller analysis at handover. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彎扭溫度整合案例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-37-k1","title":"彎扭溫度整合案例","titleEn":"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases","text":"把載重位置、溫度條件與支承狀態分成可追溯案例，確認檢測不只涵蓋正中靜載。保留各模型未處理的耦合項，交付時指出仍需更完整分析的邊界。","textEn":"Trace load location, temperature and support state through cases that extend beyond centred static loading. Retain omitted coupling mechanisms and identify boundaries requiring fuller analysis at handover.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彎扭溫度整合案例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases\" is correct?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","把載重位置、溫度條件與支承狀態分成可追溯案例，確認檢測不只涵蓋正中靜載。","跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Trace load location, temperature and support state through cases that extend beyond centred static loading.","Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把載重位置、溫度條件與支承狀態分成可追溯案例，確認檢測不只涵蓋正中靜載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trace load location, temperature and support state through cases that extend beyond centred static loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b397-v16-38","title":"彎扭溫度整合案例：定量估算","titleEn":"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彎扭溫度整合案例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彎扭溫度整合案例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases\", which statement holds?","options":["速度加倍但半徑不變時側向加速度也只增加一倍","同一站位重複量測完全一致就能保證絕對位置正確","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling speed at unchanged radius merely doubles lateral acceleration.","Identical repeated observations from one station guarantee correct absolute position.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b397-v16-39","title":"彎扭溫度整合案例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彎扭溫度整合案例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「彎扭溫度整合案例」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For combined bending, torsion and temperature cases, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「彎扭溫度整合案例」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for combined bending, torsion and temperature cases, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「彎扭溫度整合案例」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For combined bending, torsion and temperature cases, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「彎扭溫度整合案例」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for combined bending, torsion and temperature cases, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彎扭溫度整合案例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases\"?","options":["建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","幾何最大誤差一樣時所有波長的乘坐影響一定一樣"],"optionsEn":["Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal maximum geometry error gives identical ride effects at every wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b397-v16-40","title":"彎扭溫度整合案例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b397-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彎扭溫度整合案例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「彎扭溫度整合案例」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for combined bending, torsion and temperature cases. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b397-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「彎扭溫度整合案例」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for combined bending, torsion and temperature cases. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]},{"id":"b397-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彎扭溫度整合案例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Combined bending, torsion and temperature cases\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","跨度加倍時其他條件相同的梁撓度也只增加一倍"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","Doubling span with other conditions fixed merely doubles beam deflection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-hitachi-2001","v16s-hitachi-2008","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-monorail-reference","v16s-chongqing-reference"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b397-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b397-en.svg"}};
